ORIGINS -- where each added program came from==============================================================One line per program.  Companion to DOC/INDEX (what each program IS)and SOURCES.txt (licence and build method).Four origins, all public:  usenet archive   a comp.sources.games / comp.sources.misc posting                   from the late 1980s, kept as an OS-9 'ar' archive                   in a personal collection.  Named <archive>.ar.  hc disk          the same collection's other half, recovered from a                   second OS-9 disk.  Its copies are often the better                   port -- ispell and xlisp only build from these.  EFFO forum disk  European Forum for OS-9 user-group disk, from the                   Microware hobbyist archive (microware.com, OSK).  microware        the same hobbyist archive's own category trees,                   taken directly rather than through a forum disk.The C source for every one of these is on this disk under SRC/<tree>/.--------------------------------------------------------------program        SRC/        origin--------------------------------------------------------------  advcom         advint      usenet archive  advint.ar  advent         adv         usenet archive  adv.ar  advint         advint      usenet archive  advint.ar  animal         animal      usenet archive  animal.ar  ape            hc_loose    hc disk  SOURCES/USENET/ (loose C sources)  areacode       hc_utils    hc disk  SOURCES/UTILS/  (loose C sources)   [also built from misc]  ascii          misc        usenet archive  misc.ar  assembler      eff_gshell  usenet archive  eff_gshell.ar  banner         misc        usenet archive  misc.ar  bite           v_misc      hc disk  SOURCES/USENET/v_misc.ar  blackjak       effo_snobol EFFO forum disk 9   PROGRAMME/C/SNOBOL  bmgtest        strsch      usenet archive  strsch.ar  bmgtest2       strsch      usenet archive  strsch.ar  bog            bog         usenet archi